From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Order the halves of _CFInfo by byte order

_CFInfo mirrors CFRuntimeBase's 64-bit _cfinfoa as two UInt32 fields,
info and then pad. That puts info in the low half of the word only on
little-endian targets. On big-endian ones the type ID and flags of every
CF object created from Swift land in the high half, where CF does not
look for them.

Swap the fields on big-endian targets.
---
--- a/Sources/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.swift
+++ b/Sources/Foundation/NSObjCRuntime.swift
@@ -207,9 +207,15 @@
 }
 
 internal struct _CFInfo {
-    // This must match _CFRuntimeBase
+    // This must match _CFRuntimeBase, whose _cfinfoa is one 64-bit word: info
+    // is its low half and pad its high half, in memory order.
+#if _endian(big)
+    var pad : UInt32
+    var info: UInt32
+#else
     var info: UInt32
     var pad : UInt32
+#endif
     init(typeID: CFTypeID) {
         // This matches what _CFRuntimeCreateInstance does to initialize the info value
         info = UInt32((UInt32(typeID) << 8) | (UInt32(0x80)))
